.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt TIMER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm timer
.Nd a large millisecond stopwatch or countdown window, for live demonstrations
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar time
.Op Fl p
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A window that counts up from zero, to the millisecond, from the moment it
opens.
Space pauses and resumes, and so does a click; r resets; f is full
screen; q quits.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar time , Fl -countdown Ar time
Count down from
.Ar time
\(em seconds, minutes and seconds, or hours, minutes and seconds \(em and
then go on counting up in red, so an overrun shows.
.It Fl p , Fl -paused
Open stopped.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Not run for this page; it needs a desktop:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ timer -c 5:00
.Ed
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
A Wayland program cannot keep itself on top; use the window's title-bar
menu.
